<article class="env-lemma" id="083D">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/083D">Lemma <span data-tag="083D">71.6.3</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $X$ be an algebraic space over $S$. Let $Z \subset X$ be a locally principal closed subspace. Let $U = X \setminus Z$. Then $U \to X$ is an affine morphism. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The question is étale local on $X$, see Morphisms of Spaces, Lemmas <a href="/tag/03WG" data-tag="03WG">67.20.3</a> and Lemma <a href="/tag/083C" data-tag="083C">71.6.2</a>. Thus this follows from the case of schemes which is Divisors, Lemma <a href="/tag/07ZT" data-tag="07ZT">31.14.3</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>